# {{name}}: a lead plans tasks on a board; teammates work on them concurrently.
#
# The campaign lead breaks a launch request into tasks with dependencies. The market
# analyst and the copywriter each claim the ready tasks that match their capability and
# hand their results back; the lead then writes the summary. Scheduling a post waits
# for a human: the task is parked, everything else goes on, and the run pauses until
# the decision comes in.
#
#   awa validate blueprint.yaml
#   awa show blueprint.yaml --mermaid
#   awa run blueprint.yaml "Launch the analytics add-on for small businesses."
name: {{name}}
description: Plans and prepares product launch posts with an analyst and a copywriter.
version: 0.1.0

defaults:
  model: {{model}}
  max_steps: 10

agents:
  - name: campaign_lead
    description: Plans each launch on the task board and summarizes the result.
    instructions: |
      Plan the launch in one create_tasks call:
      1. key "audience", "Profile the audience", required_capabilities [analysis]: the
         description names the product and the segment from the request.
      2. key "post", "Write and schedule the post", required_capabilities [copy],
         depends_on ["audience"]: the description names the product and the channel
         (linkedin unless the request names another).
      When the results come back, answer with a short launch summary: the audience in
      one line, the post, and whether it is scheduled.
    capabilities: [coordination]

  - name: market_analyst
    description: Profiles the audience segment of a launch.
    instructions: |
      Look up the segment named in your task with lookup_segment and answer with its
      needs and the tone that works, in two lines.
    tools: [lookup_segment]
    capabilities: [analysis]

  - name: copywriter
    description: Writes launch posts and schedules them.
    instructions: |
      Write a post of at most 60 words for the product and audience in your task, then
      schedule it with schedule_post on the channel your task names. Answer with the
      post and the scheduling result.
    tools: [schedule_post]
    capabilities: [copy]

network:
  lead: campaign_lead
  teammates: [market_analyst, copywriter]
  peers: all
  limits:
    max_tasks: 6
    max_lead_turns: 6
    run_timeout: 600

approvals:
  - tool: schedule_post          # every post waits for a human

# The most one run may use, also a run a trigger starts. Options such as
# `awa run --max-requests` can only tighten it.
limits:
  max_requests: 50
  max_total_tokens: 200000
  max_duration: 5m
